<title>USA: U.S. stocks plummet, NYSE sets curbs.</title>
<headline>U.S. stocks plummet, NYSE sets curbs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. stocks were on a roller coaster ride on Thursday, with the Dow falling more than 100 points in late trading.</p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange to set curbs on index-arbitrage trading at 1451 EDT/1851 GMT.</p>
<p>The average followed bonds lower, with the long bond off 14/32 to yield 6.73 percent.</p>
